"Let $G$ be a planar multigraph of maximum degree $d$, and let $\\chi'_2(G)$ denote its strong chromatic index, the minimum number of colours in a distance-$2$ edge-colouring of $G$. Fix $\\varepsilon>0$. **Asymptotic strong chromatic-index conjecture.** For every such $G$,\n\n$$\n\\chi'_2(G) \\leq (9/2+\\varepsilon)d,\n$$\n\nprovided $d$ is sufficiently large. The examples $\\mathcal O_d$ are proposed as asymptotically extremal, and the conjecture would sharpen the known upper bound $\\limsup_{d\\to\\infty}\\chi'_2(G)/d\\leq 6$ to the constant $9/2$ for planar multigraphs."